      "description": "Gas Prices Drop Ahead of Independence Day Travel",
      "details": "Gas prices are a significant factor in discretionary spending, as they directly impact household budgets and travel costs. Ahead of the July 4th weekend, the national average for a gallon of regular gasoline dropped to $3.83, nearly 50 cents lower than a month prior. This relief at the pump likely boosted consumer confidence and willingness to spend on non-essential items like specialty food gifts, contributing to higher ROAS and lower CPA.",
